cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NovaMod, please cite the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "NovaMod: unsupervised detection of DNA/RNA modifications from nanopore signal"
abstract: >-
  NovaMod treats nanopore modification discovery as an anomaly-detection
  task. A CNN-Transformer variational autoencoder is trained on canonical
  (unmodified) signal from WGA DNA, IVT RNA, or control oligos; candidate
  modified events are then scored by reconstruction error and aggregated
  from read level to site level.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/WGLab/novamod"

# TODO: confirm the author list and ordering against the manuscript before
# the next release. Only the repository committer could be determined here.
authors:
  - family-names: "Zou"
    given-names: "Zac"
    affiliation: "Children's Hospital of Philadelphia"

keywords:
  - nanopore
  - DNA modification
  - RNA modification
  - variational autoencoder
  - anomaly detection
  - unsupervised learning

